You are assisting on ResQ Mine, an underground mine safety monitoring system (SIH26039). This is a hackathon build — prioritize working, demonstrable code over premature abstraction.

## Stack (do not suggest alternatives unless asked)
- Backend: Node.js + Express, `mqtt` npm package, `socket.io`, MongoDB via `mongoose`
- Frontend: React (functional components + hooks only, no class components), Tailwind CSS
- Simulation: plain Node.js script, no framework
- Alerts: Twilio Node SDK

## Conventions
- All MQTT topics follow `resqmine/{zoneId}/telemetry`. Never hardcode a zone ID anywhere else — read it from the payload.
- Risk-scoring logic lives in a single module (`riskEngine.js`). Do not scatter threshold checks across route handlers.
- Every MongoDB write validates the payload shape first and rejects/logs malformed data instead of throwing unhandled.
- No ML libraries (no tensorflow, no scikit-learn). Anomaly detection is intentionally rule-based for this version — do not add ML unless explicitly asked.
- Secrets (broker URL, Mongo URI, Twilio credentials) go in `.env`, never hardcoded. `.env` is gitignored.
- Keep frontend components small and named after what they show (`ZoneCard`, `ZoneDetailPanel`, `AlertLog`) — not generic (`Card1`, `Panel`).
- Comment sparingly, only where the *why* isn't obvious from the code (e.g. why a threshold value was chosen) — not restating what the code does line by line.
- Do not add authentication, user accounts, or role-based access — explicitly out of scope for this build.
- Do not add a LoRa/BLE/non-WiFi communication layer — MQTT over WiFi only, for this phase.

## When generating code
- Prefer async/await over raw promise chains.
- Prefer small, focused functions over large multi-purpose ones.
- If a request is ambiguous, default to the simplest version that satisfies `PRD.md`/`TRT.md` rather than asking — but flag the assumption in a one-line comment.
- Do not invent new MQTT topics, DB fields, or API routes beyond what's defined in `Backend-Schema.md` and `TRT.md` without flagging it as a deviation.
